Start on the most recently saved slot.

The current slot always started at 1, so after launching the game, L
(or Load in the Esc menu) loaded slot 1 rather than the game you were
playing, unless you first found your slot with PgUp/PgDn. Start on the
slot whose save file is the newest instead.

That slot holds your most recent progress, so a new game must not be
saved over it: until a game is loaded or a slot is chosen with PgUp/PgDn,
saving (S or the Esc menu) goes to the lowest free slot, with the message
"Saved to new slot N". Starting a new game (from the menu, or Enter after
Game Over) resets this.

